# Known-broken internal links inherited from the Blogger -> Hugo migration.
# Each pattern below is scoped as narrowly as the evidence allows so that a
# NEW broken link in new content still fails the check. Do not broaden these
# patterns to bare directory prefixes (e.g. "images/") -- that would also
# hide genuinely new missing images.
#
# Regenerate the error list this file was derived from with:
#   lychee --offline --no-progress --root-dir "$(pwd)/public" './public/**/*.html'

# 1) Blogger media that was never migrated into public/images/ when the blog
# moved off Blogger, e.g. images/8741533010592647710-1.png. Every such file
# in the content today carries an 18- or 19-digit Blogger post ID; the bound
# below is deliberately loosened to 15+ with no upper limit, as a buffer
# against near-variants of the same legacy shape. A new post's
# images/my-new-diagram.png does NOT match and will still fail.
# 198 of the 203 pre-existing errors are this category.
images/[0-9]{15,}-

# 2) content/blog/20230820-nexjs13.md has an /image/ (singular) vs /images/
# typo. Fixing the typo would not help: no matching file exists under
# /images/ either, so the target image is simply missing. 3 errors.
image/next-blog-13-[123]\.png

# 3) A leaked local absolute filesystem path from the author's machine,
# embedded in migrated post content (content/blog/20230907-react-native.md).
# 1 error.
/Users/alanhc/workspace/ticketing/

# 4) A protocol-relative Blogger CDN link (`//1.bp.blogspot.com/...`) left
# over from Blogger migration (content/blog/20190614-CGfinal.md). Under
# --offline mode lychee resolves the missing scheme against --root-dir and
# treats it as a local file, which will never exist. 1 error. Only shard 1
# occurs today; the digit class covers Blogger's other shards too, which is
# safe because the whole pattern is confined to a dead external domain.
[0-9]\.bp\.blogspot\.com/
